WEBVTT

00:10:57.756 --> 00:11:01.236
because at some point your qualifications
will be called into question.

00:11:01.236 --> 00:11:03.276
What would you encourage
other women to ask

00:11:03.316 --> 00:11:05.396
so that they can figure that out?

00:11:05.436 --> 00:11:09.356
G: The kinds of questions that I asked
were questions about,

00:11:09.396 --> 00:11:12.996
"Tell me, what were the criteria
that you used to make the decision?"

00:11:13.036 --> 00:11:15.076
And that was when
I eventually found it out

00:11:15.116 --> 00:11:18.516
that it really had something to do
less with performance and capability

00:11:18.516 --> 00:11:22.996
and with these, sort of, more vague things
that couldn’t be, you know, documented.

00:11:23.036 --> 00:11:25.676
So once you know what they
say the criteria are,

00:11:25.676 --> 00:11:28.516
you can certainly dig into that
and ask some more questions.

00:11:28.516 --> 00:11:30.316
But that other question about, well,